      "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
      "inputs": {
        "text": "A single complete mature European oak tree, isolated as a premium first-person exploration game vegetation asset. Use the warm, substantial natural art direction of the tree in the reference image, while redrawing the entire tree clearly at high resolution. The tree has a thick expressive irregular trunk, broad flared root collar, several individually readable exposed roots tapering outward, and strong asymmetric limbs supporting a full rounded but uneven crown. The lower trunk is substantial and cleanly visible, with warm grey-brown bark, broad sculpted grooves and restrained moss near the roots. Large coherent foliage bouquets contain many readable small oval oak leaves, dark sheltered greens inside and warmer olive greens at the outer tips, with natural open gaps revealing the main branches. The crown feels alive and three dimensional, with no spherical blobs or uniform repeated tufts. It is artist-directed, believable and tactile, with softly simplified game forms and rich surface detail, avoiding both a cartoon toy and a sparse photographic sapling. A slightly elevated three-quarter front asset view, gentle neutral diffuse lighting, no dramatic baked shadow or depth blur. The entire crown, all lateral branches and all root tips fit inside the square frame with ten percent empty margin. Plain uniform pale grey studio background. The roots end directly at the bottom of the living tree; there is no soil disc, platform, planter, landscape, rock slab or pedestal, no grass around it, no caption, no text, no grid, no additional objects and no people.",
